{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-23a-leg16/r1/sol/wi-851-df08fb7-full-review.md')\ntext='''Reviewed: df08fb7a1f15b85f4dcefe70c75d934386d55c8c\n\nVerified: Hunted fail-open held approvals first, then silent substitution of judged text and snapshot loss. The actual merge-slot, hook-step and writer tests passed for the new rule. Independently exercised the real act derivation with malformed, wrong-row and wrong-digest identities: each refused and named SR-001. No reachable fail-open or data-loss defect was demonstrated. The one targeted-suite failure reproduces in the base test before it reaches the changed judgement: Git for Windows cannot start its shell for a file-URL shallow clone (CreateFileMapping, Win32 error 5). This is an environment failure, not a lane regression. Findings below concern requirement consistency, interface declarations and consolidation.\n\nCommands:\n- \"'`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `df08fb7a1f15b85f4dcefe70c75d934386d55c8c`.\n- `git diff 31b8ed9414fbf452c6688c7b0ab9bde10bb71651...df08fb7a1f15b85f4dcefe70c75d934386d55c8c -- . '\"':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"'` (stat, path-scoped patches and name/numstat views) -> reviewed shipped changes and requirement/test deltas; no acceptance-record copy changes in the range.\n- `Get-Content` / `Select-Object` / `Select-String` and `rg -n` on CLAUDE.md, antidote, PROCESS.md, WI-851, its proposal target, rubric, changed code/tests/plan and cited registry rows -> reviewed the specified requirement surface without reading whole registries or session logs. `git status --short` -> no tracked changes. An initial PowerShell wildcard argument to rg did not expand; repeated with `rg ... docs/requirements -g '\"'*.toml'\"'`.\n- `$env:GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES = '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-23a-leg16/r1'; & 'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 2 --basetemp 'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-23a-leg16/r1/sol/wi-851' 'tests/test_held_status.py' 'tests/test_held_status_git.py' 'tests/test_text_then_act.py' 'tests/test_adjudicate_act.py' 'tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py' 'tests/test_coordinator_act.py'\"'` -> `1 failed, 240 passed in 239.88s (0:03:59)`; failed: test_a_commit_whose_parent_cannot_be_read_is_refused_by_name, during git clone, Win32 error 5.\n- `& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' 'project-trajectory/scripts/check_trajectory.py' --strict\"'` -> exit 0; `check_trajectory: clean (969 work item(s), 856 done (88%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic).`\n- `& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' 'project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py' --strict-integrity | Select-Object -Last 1\"'` -> `Traceability: SN=31 SR=138 LLR=326 TC=353 orphans=0 integrity=0 verified-mechanized=132 verified-demonstrated=6 verified-attested=0 drafts=2 budgets=4 budget-findings=0 components=4 component-findings=0 interfaces=255 interface-findings=0 ac-advisories=1 paraphrase-advisories=2.` Trace'\"'s own report output is generated by that instrument; no source was edited.\n- Inline Python through \"'`& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -B -\"'`, loading pre-fix source with `git show 31b8ed9414fbf452c6688c7b0ab9bde10bb71651:<path>` into isolated module objects -> current stale-text and missing-identity act tests PASS; each FAILS against pre-fix adjudicate_act.py, which returns an owed SR-001 re-attestation. These are behavioral assertion failures, not missing-symbol failures.\n- Inline Python loading the base test_text_then_act.py and invoking its shallow-parent test -> `BASE TEST FAIL`, same CreateFileMapping Win32 error 5 during