f identity, reservation and outcome preservation: test_the_amendment_brief_states_each_shown_rows_digest, test_bind_pending_records_the_briefs_identities and both test_record_outcome_keeps_the_identity_cell cases.\n- Retired ledger and slot arms, optional audit verdict: retirement assertions plus named/unnamed CLARITY slot test. The unnamed arm exposes the SR-228 consistency finding below.\n- Narrowed marker arm: marked/unmarked trunk, marked lane, claim/mint/telemetry writer and handback cases in test_held_status_git.\n- Unreadable/unparseable live/copy input: three real-Git cases pass and name the carrier. Shallow-parent fixture coverage remains unavailable on this host for the independently reproduced environment reason.\n- Skill wording, deferred WI-800/WI-809 references and anchored RESYNC entry: inspected; the deferred specs already cite WI-851'\"'s state rule. Dogfooded skill deltas match the shipped changes.\n- Combined sitting/re-attestation of the amended set: UNCOVERED by executable tests and not certified by this code review; process verdict records are outside the requested reading scope. Existing Approved statuses are not evidence that amended text was re-attested. Applicable released-tier authority must complete that checkpoint before landing.\n\nSemantic decisions and requirement sweep: Under PROCESS.md section 5 this is a replacement of the provenance/ledger-based selected design, with an explicit SR-208 behavior amendment, rather than a workaround retaining that design. Carry SR-208's changed claim predicate into LLR-246 and TC-241; keep SR-178/SR-179 acceptance and approval unchanged because their independent purposes remain reporting text drift and ensuring faithful copies. LLR-278 retains the independent acted-set/backing/scope decision; LLR-246 owns the independent held-authority decision; LLR-359 owns the independent reservation-to-act text-identity invariant. Further splitting their individual producer/consumer stages would add no independently valuable decision beyond those invariants. LLR-249 retains the historical advisory purpose and SR-210 unchanged; its module change carries no new approval authority. TC-278 continues to verify adjudication constraints, TC-398 verifies the new text-binding chain, and TC-241 verifies landing/marker authority; retaining these separate verification purposes is warranted. The new binding remains a witness of judged text, not a replacement acceptance anchor, so SN-029's acceptance-anchor obligation is retained. IF-196's ownership move and IF-287/IF-296's identity changes agree with their code contracts, subject to the endpoint and Data-cell findings. SR-228's unchanged audit acceptance cannot silently be weakened by deleting its child's ledger check. No other contradiction with the cited historical rows was found. This is not a stage-approval Status-change batch.\n\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:2894 -> K1, for clarity: the changed LLR-278 retires the held ledger-verdict obligation, and test_a_held_CLARITY_reattestation_bound_to_the_exact_text_lands explicitly admits an unnamed act, but its unchanged parent SR-228 acceptance at system-requirements.toml:1740 still requires that the recorded act name the verdict for audit -> explicitly reconcile SR-228's audit clause with the authorized optional-verdict behavior through its applicable amendment authority, preserving the CLARITY-only obligation, and carry that decision into LLR-278/TC-278 -> @wi-851\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/interfaces.toml:1663 -> K1: IF-129's changed digest is called by adjudicate_brief, adjudicate_act and held_status, but its Requestors still name only baseline_snapshot; IF-287 likewise omits its new held_status caller, so the declared counterpart lists do not represent the shipped relationships -> carry the new callers into IF-129 and IF-287 Requestors and record the matching semantic interface decision with this change set -> @wi-851\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/interfaces.toml:1665 -> K1: the changed Data cells of IF-129, IF-196, IF-287 and IF-296 are respectively 217, 224, 298 and 259 characters, exceeding PROCESS.md section 8's 160-character limit; these edits introduce or increase the excess and duplicate detailed contract prose that belongs beside the owner -> shorten the four cells to the allowed schema/symbol pointers and retain the detailed guarantees in their existing owner contract bodies -> @wi-851\n- [MINOR] project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py:148 -> PROCESS.md section 3 consolidation: new grep_files repeats the Git tree/index search and revision-prefix handling already implemented by kitlib.done_when._grep at line 335; fixed-string filenames versus regex matching lines and failure-versus-no-match are output/failure policies over the same shared search stage -> consolidate the common search stage in kitlib.git and have both callers select their required result and failure policy, preserving the held rule's fail-closed behavior -> @wi-851\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=4\n'''\np.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8',newline='\\\\n')\nprint(str(p))\nprint(text.splitlines()[0])\nprint(text.splitlines()[-1])\n'@ | & 'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -B -\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
